00:33:32.360 --> 00:33:38.900
When the aliens come, it's going to be the humans and all the other life forms on this planet versus the life forms from the other planet.

00:33:39.160 --> 00:33:42.320
So we gotta, you know, we gotta keep those relationships strong.

00:33:42.320 --> 00:33:50.560
Fine. And if you were remaking Ninja Crusaders, would you keep the transformations tied to the weapons or separate them so you could freely pick your form?

00:33:50.860 --> 00:33:53.500
I like it lore wise that they're tied to the weapons.

00:33:53.500 --> 00:34:00.680
I'm sure that there's, there, you could make an argument for why gameplay wise it would, uh, there'd be other ways to do it, but I, I like it.

00:34:00.960 --> 00:34:11.040
I like it because it can, it's like a balancing, uh, like you, you, you can't have the best weapon and the best animal.

00:34:11.800 --> 00:34:17.660
Um, like you always kind of have to take the drawbacks of one if you want the, the, the strengths of the other.

00:34:17.940 --> 00:34:18.900
I like that. Yeah.

00:34:19.120 --> 00:34:22.740
And if you want hard mode, you just take the staff and then you just like, no, nothing of it's good.

00:34:24.960 --> 00:34:29.920
Do the enemies feel like some kind of cohesive alien army, even with the robots?

00:34:29.920 --> 00:34:34.420
Or is it just kind of a grab bag of whatever looked cool to design for that level?

00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:37.000
That one. Okay.

00:34:37.460 --> 00:34:45.900
I think, I think aesthetically it's that one, but we, we did say earlier, at least gameplay wise that like, it doesn't feel like things are just like coming at you randomly.

00:34:45.900 --> 00:34:47.880
You didn't like, I think it's yes.

00:34:48.060 --> 00:34:48.940
Aesthetically. Yes.

00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:54.940
But the, um, but gameplay design, it is a good, it is a good, uh, cohesion.

00:34:55.320 --> 00:35:03.260
And the bosses, are they memorable or is it mostly just like a way to stop you from just moving straight in a straight line?

00:35:03.680 --> 00:35:05.020
The bosses are underwhelming.

00:35:05.020 --> 00:35:07.840
Okay. Aside from, you know, the typical, okay.

00:35:07.920 --> 00:35:13.680
The one thing that I know that the eighties and early nineties loved was to just rip off Xenomorphs.

00:35:13.760 --> 00:35:19.780
We've played enough Xenomorph things that we just, that's just what aliens were at this time.

00:35:20.060 --> 00:35:23.760
Um, so we get our token Xenomorph boss.

00:35:23.960 --> 00:35:29.580
We get some other stuff that, and it's not even just that the designs, the designs are fine.

00:35:29.580 --> 00:35:38.260
Like, aside from the Xenomorph thing, they're fine, but there's no, like the, the patterns are kind of lazy.

00:35:38.260 --> 00:36:00.060
Um, I think that if they have cut down a little bit on the insanity of enemy placement in like levels four and five and just made the bosses a bit more intricate and maybe take more than three hits to kill with, again, the staff.

00:36:00.060 --> 00:36:03.120
Um, it would have been a bit more interesting.

00:36:03.300 --> 00:36:11.300
I think when it comes to games like this, boss design is a lot more important to me than the, the, the standard enemy stuff.

00:36:11.300 --> 00:36:14.080
So it was a little disappointing on that end.

00:36:14.480 --> 00:36:23.720
Yeah. I think to me, they were the only way that they were memorable was that they were manageable, um, which I do appreciate compared to other games.

00:36:23.740 --> 00:36:27.000
But yeah, I mean, like they were just, you know, standard bosses.

00:36:27.420 --> 00:36:30.560
Uh, I did like that UFO boss battle though.

00:36:31.040 --> 00:36:41.180
Hey, you can only attack it from one side, which is kind of strange because it's like, it's the same area where the hip, like the hip box is always on the left side of these monsters, uh, for whatever reason.

00:36:41.180 --> 00:36:43.680
But the, this is a UFO that's symmetrical.

00:36:43.960 --> 00:36:48.340
So theoretically, whatever weak spot you're attacking should be on the other side as well.

00:36:48.540 --> 00:36:52.040
But I liked that it sped up as the fight went on.

00:36:52.180 --> 00:36:56.100
And, uh, you know, again, if you know what you're doing, you probably take these things down before this even happens.

00:36:56.120 --> 00:37:01.940
But the, the projectiles of it and the speed of it never, it was never cheap.

00:37:01.940 --> 00:37:11.000
It was dodgeable and it was, you were able to anticipate it, but it also made it somewhat of a more interesting fight than these other ones that were just like, here's a creepy alien monster on.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:18.320
And wheels. Also, and this is something I, like, while I was playing the game, didn't notice.

00:37:18.320 --> 00:37:33.460
Like, I, I thought that there were like 10 actual stages and not just like broken up into areas of five tech, technically five stages with each one getting a dash one and a dash two to count for the 10.

00:37:33.460 --> 00:37:46.240
And it doesn't really feel like, even, even if you die over and over again, like, it doesn't feel by the time you get to stage five that you've made any actual progress into the alien, like, world.

00:37:46.920 --> 00:37:57.900
I will say, I didn't, I didn't finish stage five, but just watching the let's play here, um, while we're, while we're recording this, I saw the end screen come up and I was like, wait, it's over?

00:37:58.200 --> 00:38:00.680
Like it just, the final boss didn't even look like a final boss.

00:38:00.740 --> 00:38:06.440
It just felt like, yeah, it didn't feel like it got grand and became like this, this grandiose ending.

00:38:06.440 --> 00:38:16.160
Yeah, the only real, um, indication that you get that this is the final boss, because he's not big, um, is that he has two forms.

00:38:16.180 --> 00:38:20.560
Like he has his body and then he's got his skeleton.

00:38:21.060 --> 00:38:28.260
Um, and other than that, like, I wouldn't have thought that this is, that this is end boss material here.

00:38:28.440 --> 00:38:30.060
Like I said, kind of disappointing design.

00:38:30.760 --> 00:38:33.220
Yeah, and it just doesn't really feel like you're going on a journey.

00:38:33.220 --> 00:38:41.320
It's kind of like you, you started, you started in town and then you just went to the next town over and it's like, hey, that's where the aliens are.

00:38:42.680 --> 00:38:45.180
You know, it's like part one of an adventure.

00:38:45.800 --> 00:38:57.620
Yeah. Uh, you know, you should, you should probably, especially with the UFO thing in the fourth stage, it's like, then it's time to, again, do a contra thing and get like, get kind of crazy with it.

00:38:57.620 --> 00:39:07.380
Like the, now all of a sudden it's like kind of unsettling the area you're in and it's more alien and it's like the, there's, there's heads coming out of the walls and shit.

00:39:07.380 --> 00:39:08.800
It's like, that never happens.

00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:17.500
Um, and the boss designs, you know, we talked about like gameplay wise, but they're also just weak designs compared to like the regular enemies.

00:39:18.300 --> 00:39:25.320
Yeah. There's one that's got a little like googly, like, like little like spindly arms.

00:39:25.480 --> 00:39:26.400
It's kind of funny looking.

00:39:27.760 --> 00:39:32.780
And now that you've mentioned this, these levels, I'm like thinking back to it all.

00:39:32.980 --> 00:39:37.560
And I wonder like, are you supposed, is it supposed to be like, you're just trying to get to this big bad?

00:39:37.660 --> 00:39:40.040
Like, what is the reason you're in each of these levels?

00:39:40.180 --> 00:39:42.720
Cause it's like, Hey, you're in the city and then you're in underwater.

00:39:42.720 --> 00:39:45.840
Then you're in the Canyon. And then you're in a castle, like an old fashioned castle.

00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:47.480
Then you're in an aircraft carrier.

00:39:47.520 --> 00:39:51.640
Like were these all just like in your path or like, did you have to go there for something?

00:39:51.740 --> 00:39:54.760
Was there like a, were there like five people you needed to take out?

00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:59.980
Or, you know, is that explained in the manual or is it like, is this one straight line adventure?

00:40:00.340 --> 00:40:02.580
Or are there five missions that have to be completed to win?

00:40:02.880 --> 00:40:03.960
Things I need to know.

00:40:04.260 --> 00:40:05.960
We'll never, we'll never know.

00:40:06.240 --> 00:40:08.560
Well, until the movie comes out, the reboot.

00:40:09.100 --> 00:40:10.200
Movie we make.

00:40:10.820 --> 00:40:15.020
There were, there were no sequels for Ninja Crusaders.

00:40:15.340 --> 00:40:21.380
It's one and done. And maybe the reason why Joe thought this was a shmup was because the developer.

00:40:21.380 --> 00:40:22.620
I didn't, Sean said.

00:40:23.220 --> 00:40:24.060
Oh, right, right.

00:40:24.220 --> 00:40:26.260
No, no, no. Joe said it.

00:40:26.580 --> 00:40:39.540
Oh, right, right. The reason Joe said that this was a shmup is because NMK, the developer, they basically like abandoned this and moved on to arcade shooters like Thunder Dragon, Blackheart.

00:40:40.120 --> 00:40:48.300
And what I'm going to probably botch here is Hakka Mecha Fighter, which doesn't really sound, it sounds like a fighting game, but it is a shmup, I confirmed.

00:40:48.300 --> 00:40:50.860
So these, these games, I looked at them.

00:40:50.860 --> 00:40:52.360
They're all shmups.

00:40:53.060 --> 00:40:56.000
Absolutely. They do the things that you expect shmups to do.

